      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-1-6 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
